WEBVTT

00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:14.490
<b>Rumble</b>

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:20.870
Look!

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:24.180
It's a peach-shaped boxed lunch.

00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:26.380
Bobbing, bobbing down the river...

00:00:26.860 --> 00:00:28.280
Peach!

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.630
Bobbing, bobbing...

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.370
Peach, peach!

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.250
<i>Coming home to Kagawa 
was the right choice, after all.</i>

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:51.690
<b>Poco's Udon World</b>

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:14.480
<b>Tawara Noodles</b>

00:02:11.150 --> 00:02:14.150
Episode 7: "Ritsurin Garden"

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:16.360
One, two, three!

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:23.780
No, listen. I turned in

00:02:24.190 --> 00:02:25.660
my resignation at work.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.990
Really?! You really quit?

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:31.210
Well... I guess that's what it comes down to.

00:02:31.210 --> 00:02:33.670
"You guess"? Are you gonna be okay?

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:35.460
I'll get by.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:37.650
Gao! Gao!

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:38.950
I plan on doing the same job here, 
just as a freelancer.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:41.970
I still have to look after Poco 
for the time being, anyway...

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.410
"For the time being"...

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:45.780
Did you talk with his parents?

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.180
Let's just say it's a long story...

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:51.880
And I've decided to live here 
with Poco for a little while.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.060
Gao! Gao!

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:53.850
Wait, Souta!

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:56.440
Right now, I'm all he has.

00:02:57.420 --> 00:02:59.380
Well... This isn't somethin' 
to discuss on the phone.

00:02:59.380 --> 00:03:01.600
I'll come by again sometime soon.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:03.290
Okay. Talk to you later.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.570
<i>Good job!</i>

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:07.990
So now you're unemployed, huh?

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:10.450
I'm not! I went freelance, that's all.

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:12.210
Apologize to all the freelancers in Japan!

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:14.210
Are you gonna find any gigs in Kagawa?

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.590
I can get work from my previous 
job for a little while.

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:20.030
That won't last forever.

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:21.660
But it's enough for now.

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:24.890
I got introduced to an 
agency on Shodoshima, too.

00:03:24.890 --> 00:03:26.750
An agency on Shodoshima?

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:27.600
Yeah.

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:30.800
Dahama-san from my previous job 
put me in touch with them.

00:03:31.070 --> 00:03:33.240
Well, whatever works.

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.770
But you oughta look for clients here.

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:37.720
I will, in time.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:44.360
Anyhow, it's about time I got back to work.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:45.370
See ya.

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:46.370
See ya!

00:03:46.770 --> 00:03:48.240
Don't imitate me.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:51.210
Nakaji, bye-bye!

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:53.110
Shall we go back inside?

00:04:03.860 --> 00:04:06.000
What to make for dinner...

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.960
We had udon for lunch...

00:04:09.010 --> 00:04:12.060
Wait, am I really spending all day 
worrying about and preparing meals?

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:14.310
Oh, that reminds me.

00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:16.940
Poco, want to go buy a watermelon?

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:20.690
Huh? Poco?

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:24.130
Poco!

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:26.130
Poco?

00:04:29.700 --> 00:04:31.410
Poco! Where are you going?!

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:32.710
Granny!

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.700
Huh? Granny's house?

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:35.820
All by yourself?

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:38.840
I guess it's only next door...

00:04:38.840 --> 00:04:40.090
Okay. Be careful.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.820
Okay!

00:04:43.280 --> 00:04:45.220
<i>Going out all by himself...</i>

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:47.100
<i>He's growing up.</i>

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:57.330
What to make for dinner...

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:00.020
I cook, eat, clean,

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.680
then turn around and 
cook, eat, and clean again,

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:05.300
then go to sleep, get up, 
and cook, eat, and...

00:05:04.090 --> 00:05:05.300
Souta!

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:07.410
Souta.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.660
Welcome home, Poco. Took a while, huh?

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:11.120
Howdy-do?

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:14.360
H-Hello.

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:17.710
Here I thought you went on back to Tokyo.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.000
I did,

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:23.210
but as it turns out, 
I'm going to live here now.

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:25.710
With your secret love child?

00:05:25.710 --> 00:05:28.090
You really want him to be 
a love child, don't you?

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:30.360
Here. I chilled some watermelon.

00:05:31.280 --> 00:05:33.410
Poco, did you hear that? Watermelon!

00:05:33.410 --> 00:05:35.480
Yeah! Watermelon!

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:49.370
Is it hard to eat? Want me to 
pick out the seeds for you?

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:50.970
Give it here.

00:05:57.570 --> 00:05:59.290
Watch closely, now.

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:00.690
This is what ya do with the seeds!

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:10.870
D-Did you pick this watermelon 
from your fields?

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:12.290
That I did.

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:15.930
I tend to the fields as a hobby, 
though I only grow a little.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:18.520
Seems like there's been

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:20.630
somethin' in my fields again lately.

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:23.510
Got myself a vegetable thief, 
or maybe a wild boar...

00:06:24.130 --> 00:06:25.190
Or maybe a tanuki?

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:29.630
Whatever it is, I'm afraid it's too fast for me...

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:31.200
Oh... Really?

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:34.080
Well, I sure am surprised you decided

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:36.530
to move back to the countryside.

00:06:36.530 --> 00:06:38.520
Well, it's a long story.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:43.450
I guess everyone wants to go up to Tokyo once.

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:47.090
I definitely wanted to experience Tokyo, yes.

00:06:47.800 --> 00:06:50.650
My granddaughter says the same thing.

00:06:50.950 --> 00:06:53.380
Though her father says there ain't no reason

00:06:53.380 --> 00:06:55.790
for her to leave the prefecture.

00:06:57.850 --> 00:06:59.530
It was the same with my family.

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:03.120
He's probably worried about his daughter.

00:07:03.970 --> 00:07:05.690
<i>I can understand that now.</i>

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:08.900
Please tell your granddaughter that

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.900
she should really talk it over with him.

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:12.930
Like ya know everything....

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:14.270
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:16.340
I got a little full of myself.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:20.410
Watermelon, yummy!

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:22.640
It really is, isn't it?

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:35.470
<b>Tawara Noodles</b>

00:07:32.710 --> 00:07:35.470
Poco! Dinner's ready!

00:07:38.110 --> 00:07:39.270
Gaogao!

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:42.520
P-Poco! You can't draw on the walls!

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:44.360
No draw?

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:45.460
Crayon...

00:07:45.760 --> 00:07:47.520
That's never going to come off, is it?

00:07:51.030 --> 00:07:52.660
<b>Manabe-san 
Incoming Call</b>

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:55.270
Hello? Manabe-san?

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:56.780
Sorry for callin' out of the blue.

00:07:56.780 --> 00:07:58.490
I'm not interruptin', am I?

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:02.730
No, actually, I was just feeling 
one of the pains of parenting...

00:08:02.730 --> 00:08:06.710
Were ya? I wanted to check up on ya.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:10.530
Thanks. Actually, I decided 
to come back to Kagawa.

00:08:10.530 --> 00:08:11.950
Really? You did?

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:12.650
Yeah.

00:08:12.650 --> 00:08:14.700
You mean you're gonna live here?

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:18.090
Yeah, for a while yet. Poco, too.

00:08:18.310 --> 00:08:20.430
Oh, really!

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:24.140
Oh, in that case, do ya have time tomorrow?

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:25.460
You and Poco-chan?

00:08:25.460 --> 00:08:26.580
Yeah, we're free...

00:08:26.580 --> 00:08:30.000
There's gonna be a Gaogao-chan 
show at Ritsurin Garden!

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:33.040
But I hafta take Eitarou for a 
checkup in the afternoon...

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:35.450
Oh, should I take the kids, then?

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:36.740
Poco would love it.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:37.800
Would you really?

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:39.950
<b>Sanuki Udon
Ueharaya</b>

00:08:38.200 --> 00:08:39.950
<b>Open</b>

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:42.710
Sorry about this.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:46.830
I feel like I'm makin' ya babysit Nozomi...

00:08:46.830 --> 00:08:48.120
It's no trouble.

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:51.560
Poco will have a lot more fun 
with Nozomi-chan there, too.

00:08:51.560 --> 00:08:52.720
It's a big help!

00:08:53.930 --> 00:08:55.910
She's so tan.

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:57.720
We've been goin' to the pool a lot.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:01.690
Still, I really wasn't expectin' you

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:03.980
to move back to Kagawa.

00:09:04.270 --> 00:09:07.420
Well... I have a lot to think through...

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:08.410
Hot!

00:09:08.690 --> 00:09:10.910
It's hot, so make sure you blow on it, okay?

00:09:12.810 --> 00:09:15.460
You're like a real family.

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:18.990
Speaking of which, Senpai, I need your advice!

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:21.120
S-Senpai?

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:24.920
Oh, he's drawin' on the walls?

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:27.090
Right... And I don't know

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:27.420
Yummy!

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:29.460
the best way to handle scolding.

00:09:28.450 --> 00:09:31.670
Ta-da! It's a big deep-fried tofu!

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:33.170
Drip, drop, drip!

00:09:32.660 --> 00:09:33.170
Nozomi.

00:09:33.920 --> 00:09:36.060
We don't play with our food, remember?

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:38.630
That's it! That intimidating air!

00:09:39.490 --> 00:09:40.510
What do ya mean?

00:09:40.860 --> 00:09:44.080
Oh, uh, I mean, like... 
The authority of a parent?

00:09:44.380 --> 00:09:47.060
I don't think I have enough of that.

00:09:49.360 --> 00:09:52.160
You do hafta scold 'em when 
they do something wrong.

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:54.510
But just yellin' won't change their behavior.

00:09:54.810 --> 00:09:58.320
So I'd say the most important 
thing is to always explain it.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:02.270
Another strategy is to try an' 
come up with creative workarounds.

00:10:02.270 --> 00:10:04.830
S-Senpai... You're so dependable...

00:10:05.240 --> 00:10:07.940
Everybody goes through the 
"drawin' on the walls" stage.

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:09.630
Nozomi did it a lot, too.

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:11.280
Do not!

00:10:11.280 --> 00:10:13.930
That's right. You don't anymore, do you?

00:10:14.420 --> 00:10:17.220
I bet you drew on walls too, right, Tawara-kun?

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:20.070
Me? I wonder...

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:23.030
Hey! My deep-fried tofu!

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:24.120
Yummy, yummy!

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:26.230
Poco!

00:10:26.680 --> 00:10:28.720
Never let your guard down, "Dad"!

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:32.730
<b>Special Place of Scenic Beauty: Ritsurin Garden Map</b>

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:36.780
I really am sorry for askin' 
you to look after Nozomi.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.290
Call it my thank you for the advice.

00:10:38.290 --> 00:10:40.360
It was nothin' that special.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:41.490
Really, though...

00:10:42.050 --> 00:10:44.770
Poco seems to have a lot of fun 
playing with Nozomi-chan.

00:10:44.770 --> 00:10:46.270
Isn't this great, Poco?

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:49.580
We're gonna go see Gaogao-chan 
with Nozomi-chan!

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:55.750
Okay, I'll call ya as soon as 
Eitarou's checkup is over.

00:10:56.030 --> 00:10:57.550
Okay. Have a safe trip.

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:59.550
Nozomi, you be good, now!

00:10:59.850 --> 00:11:01.820
'Kay! Bye-bye!

00:11:05.050 --> 00:11:07.770
There's still some time before the show.

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:09.890
Shall we have a look around?

00:11:09.890 --> 00:11:10.620
'Kay!

00:11:10.620 --> 00:11:11.340
'Kay!

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:17.720
What is this? It's so big an' weird!

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:20.530
I think she's called Hoko-san.

00:11:21.550 --> 00:11:23.280
Oh, wow!

00:11:23.830 --> 00:11:25.910
So many different souvenirs...

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:29.410
What are these?! They look really modern!

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:31.430
I think I like it...

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:35.700
They're wood-carved daruma dolls.
A young woman makes them.

00:11:35.700 --> 00:11:37.670
We have hand towels, too.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:39.510
The hand towels are trendy, too!

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:44.010
<b>I'm sorry. 
I'm sorry. 
I'm sorry.</b>

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:44.010
<b>I was only 
expecting 
boring, 
stereotypical souvenirs.</b>

00:11:39.730 --> 00:11:42.250
<i>I was only expecting boring, 
stereotypical souvenirs.</i>

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:43.760
<i>I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.</i>

00:11:47.460 --> 00:11:51.130
Poco-chan, hold my hand so you don't fall!

00:11:51.130 --> 00:11:52.290
Hand!

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:54.150
That's nice of you, Nozomi-chan.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:56.070
Uh-huh! I'm a big girl now!

00:11:56.940 --> 00:11:59.320
She acted like a spoiled baby not so long ago...

00:12:00.210 --> 00:12:02.450
Nozomi-chan's growing up fast, too.

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:04.120
Go slow, okay?

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:07.620
Mister!

00:12:07.740 --> 00:12:11.910
<b>Mister</b>

00:12:07.980 --> 00:12:09.020
<i>"Mister"?!</i>

00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:10.790
<i>Ah, it had been a while...</i>

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:12.680
There's a bunch of fish swimmin'!

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:16.310
Right, those are koi.

00:12:16.310 --> 00:12:17.880
You're cryin'?

00:12:18.180 --> 00:12:20.090
My heart's just a little hurt...

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:23.670
What do koi eat?

00:12:23.670 --> 00:12:24.600
Udon?

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:27.300
Want to feed them?

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:29.680
<b>One for 80 Yen, Two for 150 Yen 
Koi Food
Two for 150 Yen</b>

00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:31.960
It's so long!

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:32.940
Long!

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:35.450
It doesn't hurt!

00:12:36.130 --> 00:12:36.940
Doesn't hurt!

00:12:37.230 --> 00:12:38.840
It doesn't hurt!

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:39.980
Doesn't hurt!

00:12:42.030 --> 00:12:45.140
Hey! Those aren't for hitting people!

00:12:45.140 --> 00:12:46.200
No bullying!

00:12:46.600 --> 00:12:48.830
Watch. You break it off like this and...

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:49.410
There.

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:54.960
It ate it!

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:55.570
Ate it!

00:12:55.570 --> 00:12:56.940
I wanna try!

00:12:56.070 --> 00:12:57.520
Yummy, yummy!

00:12:57.520 --> 00:12:59.960
Break it into pieces small 
enough for them to eat, okay?

00:13:04.040 --> 00:13:05.690
Lots of koi came over!

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:06.720
Lots!

00:13:11.420 --> 00:13:13.260
That's a lot of fish...

00:13:14.710 --> 00:13:15.570
Poco!

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:20.200
That's kind of terrifying...

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:22.730
If I fall in, will they eat me, too?

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:26.150
It's okay! You don't have to worry about that!

00:13:29.610 --> 00:13:31.790
Good thing the koi didn't eat us, huh?

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:33.290
Dumplings are yummy!

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:34.470
Yummy!

00:13:34.470 --> 00:13:35.530
All right!

00:13:35.530 --> 00:13:37.780
Now that the dumplings cheered us back up...

00:13:37.780 --> 00:13:39.540
Ready to go see Gaogao-chan?

00:13:40.050 --> 00:13:41.430
Gaogao!

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:49.010
<b>Gaogao-chan Show</b>

00:13:42.770 --> 00:13:44.400
Hurry! Hurry!

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:45.570
Hurry!

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:47.420
I'm coming, I'm coming.

00:13:49.380 --> 00:13:51.880
Look at this crowd...

00:13:51.880 --> 00:13:54.020
Gaogao-chan really is popular.

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:56.910
Gaogao-chan!

00:13:56.910 --> 00:13:59.830
As far as they're concerned, 
the show's already started...

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:02.650
A DJ booth?

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:04.200
Wow...

00:14:04.750 --> 00:14:06.150
It's the guy from Tawara Noodles!

00:14:07.020 --> 00:14:08.210
Hello!

00:14:08.210 --> 00:14:09.080
Hello.

00:14:09.080 --> 00:14:10.660
Eh... Oh, hello.

00:14:11.000 --> 00:14:13.450
Aren't you the priest I met... Um...

00:14:13.450 --> 00:14:15.070
Yes, I am Fujiyama.

00:14:15.070 --> 00:14:18.040
Two little ones with you today? 
Looks like fun!

00:14:18.320 --> 00:14:21.060
Yeah... I'm watching a friend's child.

00:14:21.060 --> 00:14:22.520
I see...

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:24.150
So what's goin' on with the restaurant?

00:14:24.150 --> 00:14:25.090
Did you reopen it?!

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:28.470
I'm sorry. Honestly, 
I don't plan on reopening it.

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:30.220
Oh, okay...

00:14:31.580 --> 00:14:34.060
Um... May I ask why you're here today?

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:37.080
Also, do you two know each other?

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:38.600
Oh, he's my older brother.

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:41.520
My sister really loved

00:14:41.520 --> 00:14:44.110
the udon at Tawara Noodles.

00:14:46.240 --> 00:14:47.490
Tanuki!

00:14:47.740 --> 00:14:49.840
Yep! That's a tanuki!

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:52.730
My brother is absolutely 
infatuated with tanuki.

00:14:52.730 --> 00:14:54.740
He collects all kinds of 
merchandise and books.

00:14:55.380 --> 00:15:00.370
This area is absolutely 
inseparable from tanuki.

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:04.630
Are you also interested 
in tanuki, Tawara-san?

00:15:04.940 --> 00:15:06.910
Oh, no, not especially...

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:08.630
Tanuki! Tanuki!

00:15:06.910 --> 00:15:08.020
Oh, right!

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:12.010
My brother's the stage DJ for 
the Gaogao-chan show today!

00:15:12.530 --> 00:15:15.060
You'll be seeing a different side

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:17.640
of me than you saw the other day.

00:15:18.150 --> 00:15:19.380
A DJ?

00:15:23.570 --> 00:15:26.740
Far away on the edge of space, in Galaxy M87,

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:30.020
there lived a terrifying alien

00:15:29.700 --> 00:15:31.530
He's like a different person...

00:15:30.020 --> 00:15:32.740
bent on invading Earth.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:36.900
His name is Ipalnemoani Gaogao,

00:15:34.740 --> 00:15:37.260
Gaogao!

00:15:36.020 --> 00:15:38.580
Ipalne... What did he say?

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:41.120
and he is said to be the most 
fearsome alien in the universe.

00:15:38.580 --> 00:15:41.580
Sorry. I couldn't hear it, either.

00:15:41.760 --> 00:15:47.840
<i>He came from the edge of the universe!</i>

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:53.300
<i>I am Gaogao-chan!</i>

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:53.300
I am Gaogao-chan!

00:15:54.600 --> 00:16:00.850
<i>The scar on his back is 
the mark of a champion!</i>

00:16:01.320 --> 00:16:02.440
<i>One, two, three!</i>

00:16:01.790 --> 00:16:03.210
Sae-san, too?

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:07.500
<i>The neighborhood's peace</i>

00:16:07.500 --> 00:16:10.780
<i>is always, always...</i>

00:16:10.780 --> 00:16:13.560
<i>at the limit!</i>

00:16:14.690 --> 00:16:17.090
<i>The eyes! Aim for the eyes!</i>

00:16:17.890 --> 00:16:18.410
Gao!

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:19.290
Gao!

00:16:19.680 --> 00:16:20.870
Gao! Gao!

00:16:22.790 --> 00:16:24.210
<i>Gao!</i>

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:27.310
That was so much fun!

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:28.670
G-Gaogao-chan!

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:32.180
<i>Am I losing my stamina?</i>

00:16:32.180 --> 00:16:34.240
<i>Also, those siblings...</i>

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:34.930
<i>What an enigma.</i>

00:16:35.160 --> 00:16:37.030
Poco-chan, let's play over there!

00:16:37.030 --> 00:16:39.010
Hold my hand!

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:40.160
Hand!

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:46.250
Nozomi-chan got more mature 
in the blink of an eye.

00:16:46.250 --> 00:16:50.030
Are they both going to keep growing up?

00:16:51.190 --> 00:16:54.400
Anyway, I was right to come back to Kagawa.

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:57.700
Poco livened up the instant we got back.

00:16:58.010 --> 00:17:00.890
Mister! The park's really big!

00:17:00.890 --> 00:17:02.180
Big!

00:17:02.180 --> 00:17:05.230
A long time ago, there was a zoo next door, too.

00:17:05.230 --> 00:17:06.730
They had lions!

00:17:07.160 --> 00:17:08.040
Lions!

00:17:08.040 --> 00:17:09.230
Lions?

00:17:09.230 --> 00:17:10.500
Gao!

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:22.270
Tawara-kun, thanks so much for today.

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:23.520
You were a lifesaver.

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:25.100
Oh, not at all. Anytime.

00:17:25.100 --> 00:17:28.300
If you ever need some help 
yourself, just let me know.

00:17:25.820 --> 00:17:26.810
Gao!

00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:30.480
Senpai, I'll be counting on you!

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:32.960
It feels so surreal.

00:17:32.960 --> 00:17:36.190
We were classmates, 
and now we're "mom friends"!

00:17:36.190 --> 00:17:38.540
Yep, that's how it feels...

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:42.240
<b>Tawara Noodles</b>

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:42.240
Okay, we'll put it here.

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:43.330
Stick!

00:17:43.330 --> 00:17:44.230
Stick!

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:45.070
Stick!

00:17:45.370 --> 00:17:46.000
Stick!

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:49.660
There! You can draw as much 
as you want on this spot.

00:17:49.660 --> 00:17:52.070
But no drawing on the walls! Got it?

00:17:52.070 --> 00:17:53.320
Got it!

00:17:53.320 --> 00:17:54.940
Okay. Here are your crayons.

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:56.010
'Kay.

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:01.140
Koi.

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:02.510
Gaogao-chan.

00:18:05.570 --> 00:18:07.900
Now that I think about it, I did...

00:18:12.690 --> 00:18:13.610
<b>Tawara Souta</b>

00:18:16.430 --> 00:18:18.640
<i>Of all things, it would be a lion, huh?</i>

00:18:38.790 --> 00:18:41.450
<i>Dad had it rough, too, didn't he?</i>

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:44.610
<i>I can't believe I never realized it until now.</i>

00:18:45.730 --> 00:18:47.860
<i>When I told him I was leaving for Tokyo,</i>

00:18:48.650 --> 00:18:50.350
<i>I should've talked it out with him more.</i>

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:52.870
Do what ya want.

00:18:54.520 --> 00:18:55.700
Souta.

00:18:57.100 --> 00:18:58.170
Sleepy.

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.990
Oh, right. We'd better go to bed.

00:19:01.420 --> 00:19:02.200
Gaogao?

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:04.680
This? It's a lion.

00:19:04.980 --> 00:19:08.450
My dad did his best to clean it up, 
but it looks like he couldn't get it off.

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:09.710
Gao!

00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:34.980
<b>Hamada-san 
Incoming call</b>

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:34.160
Dahama-san?

00:19:35.130 --> 00:19:46.910
<b>Gaogao-chan Exercises</b>

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:39.700
<i>Far away on the edge of space, in Galaxy M87,</i>

00:19:37.050 --> 00:19:46.910
<b>Lyrics: Shinomaru Nodoka              Composition: Hashimoto Yukari</b>

00:19:40.130 --> 00:19:42.990
<i>there lived a terrifying alien</i>

00:19:42.990 --> 00:19:45.550
<i>bent on invading Earth.</i>

00:19:45.850 --> 00:19:49.210
<i>His name is Ipalnemoani Gaogao,</i>

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:52.090
<i>and he is said to be the most</i>

00:19:52.090 --> 00:19:54.290
<i>fearsome alien in the universe.</i>

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:13.960
<b>Gaogao-chan and</b>

00:21:10.870 --> 00:21:13.960
<b>The Blue Sky</b>

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:18.990
<i>The Tale of Gaogao-chan and Upbringing!</i>

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:19.960
<b>Episode 7: 
"Gaogao-chan and Upbringing"</b>

00:21:20.860 --> 00:21:24.770
<i>Mimi and Momo are looking after</i>

00:21:24.770 --> 00:21:27.090
<i>the neighborhood hedgehog family's babies.</i>

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:30.100
<i>Aww, they're so cute!</i>

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:32.470
<i>And a little prickly!</i>

00:21:32.800 --> 00:21:36.400
<i>Would Earthlings call even 
scrubbing brushes "cute"?</i>

00:21:38.140 --> 00:21:39.480
<i>Hello?</i>

00:21:39.730 --> 00:21:41.860
<i>Gao? You want me to babysit?</i>

00:21:42.270 --> 00:21:45.400
<i>We got an urgent call and have to go out.</i>

00:21:45.700 --> 00:21:46.710
<i>Sorry!</i>

00:21:46.710 --> 00:21:48.850
<i>You can do it, Gaogao-chan!</i>

00:21:48.850 --> 00:21:52.160
<i>You have spikes, too. You look 
like you could be their daddy!</i>

00:21:57.680 --> 00:21:59.590
<i>Will they really be okay?</i>

00:21:59.590 --> 00:22:00.720
<i>Don't worry!</i>

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:04.890
<i>I know Gaogao-chan can help make 
those little hedgehogs strong.</i>

00:22:19.960 --> 00:22:23.070
<i>Lion cubs become stronger</i>

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:24.770
<i>by being dropped off of cliffs.</i>

00:22:28.300 --> 00:22:29.070
<i>Chestnuts?</i>

00:22:34.950 --> 00:22:38.680
<i>Gao!</i>

